      <!-- Right Column: Headline, Bio, Credentials, Contact -->
      <div class="about-right">
        <div>
          <h3 class="about-headline"><em>Clinician who codes</em> — building practical clinical decision support systems.</h3>
        </div>

        <div class="about-bio" style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1rem;">
          <p>
            I am an Internal Medicine Resident at RSUP Prof. Dr. I.G.N.G. Ngoerah / Udayana University in Denpasar, Bali. My daily clinical practice and research endeavors center around internal medicine care—with special clinical interest in <strong>hematology</strong> and <strong>gastroenterology</strong>.
          </p>
          <p>
            Born from immediate friction encountered at the bedside, across inpatient wards, and in high-acuity emergency rooms, I build clinical decision support systems (CDSS) engineered to help clinicians make evidence-grounded decisions swiftly, accurately, and safely.
          </p>
          <p style="color: #94A3B8; font-style: italic; border-left: 2px solid var(--accent-cyan); padding-left: 1rem; margin-top: 0.25rem;">
            "I believe the most impactful healthcare innovations emerge at the intersection of clinical care precision and code efficiency."
          </p>
        </div>

